codemap 8
path reader-gui
kind flow
author ai
group gui
note The human's surface as one frame. There is no retained widget tree: every frame the App polls the background work, turns the frame's keys into actions, then builds the element tree for the whole window from the Model - top bar, docked panels, the centre tab, status bar, tooltip - and hands it to the layout and the renderer. A view never changes the Model: it takes &Model, and a click pushes an Action onto the frame's queue; apply runs the queue once the tree is built, so apply is the one place state changes during a frame. Editing is limited to what a reader needs - deleting a step or a path, pinning a selection from the listing, creating an empty path - and everything else is typed into the output panel as a CLI command. gui-structure lists the rules the modules keep.

